        "thread_id": "TH2",
        "thread_goal": "Define practical staging, storage, and handling rules for different product types.",
        "messages": [
          {
            "msg_id": "M19",
            "speaker_id": 27468,
            "reply_to": null,
            "text": "Hi all, for T2, I've drafted a proposal for our storage and labeling method. The idea is to use the shelving unit near the back exit. We can zone it by order type: A for ambient, B for bulky, C for chilled. For labels, a simple format: Order #, Customer Name, and Pickup Date. Thoughts?",
            "mentions": [
              128135,
              213765,
              140484
            ],
            "artifact_refs": [
              "T2"
            ],
            "decision_refs": [],
            "reactions": []
          },
          {
            "msg_id": "M20",
            "speaker_id": 128135,
            "reply_to": "M19",
            "text": "Zone B for bulky works. How many shelves can we use? Some of the electronics boxes are big. We need to make sure we don't block the walkway.",
            "mentions": [
              27468
            ],
            "artifact_refs": [],
            "decision_refs": [],
            "reactions": []
          },
          {
            "msg_id": "M21",
            "speaker_id": 213765,
            "reply_to": "M19",
            "text": "What about flowers? They can't just sit on a dry shelf. For T6, they need to be in a bucket with water and away from direct sunlight. We have that small area by the garden center entrance, maybe we can use that?",
            "mentions": [
              27468
            ],
            "artifact_refs": [
              "T6"
            ],
            "decision_refs": [],
            "reactions": []
          },
          {
            "msg_id": "M22",
            "speaker_id": 140484,
            "reply_to": "M19",
            "text": "I like the simple A-B-C zoning. For the labels, can we add the number of pieces? Like '1 of 2', '2 of 2'. It helps prevent mistakes. My experience with bakery orders is that things can get separated easily.",
            "mentions": [
              27468
            ],
            "artifact_refs": [],
            "decision_refs": [],
            "reactions": [
              {
                "emoji": "+1",
                "count": 2
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "msg_id": "M23",
            "speaker_id": 27468,
            "reply_to": "M20",
            "text": "Good point. We can dedicate the bottom two shelves for Zone B, that should keep the aisle clear. We'll need to make sure the handling guidelines in A3 specify no stacking for fragile electronics.",
            "mentions": [
              128135
            ],
            "artifact_refs": [
              "A3"
            ],
            "decision_refs": [],
            "reactions": []
          },
          {
            "msg_id": "M24",
            "speaker_id": 27468,
            "reply_to": "M21",
            "text": "Yes, that makes sense. We can create a separate zone, Zone F (for Floral), in that location. We should document this in the main procedure and create the specific instructions for A4. Thanks for catching that.",
            "mentions": [
              213765
            ],
            "artifact_refs": [
              "A4"
            ],
            "decision_refs": [],
            "reactions": []
          },
          {
            "msg_id": "M25",
            "speaker_id": 27468,
            "reply_to": "M22",
            "text": "Adding 'piece count' to the label is a great idea. It will definitely help with the handover checklist in A8. So the label will have: Order #, Name, Pickup Date, and Piece Count (e.g., 1/2).",
            "mentions": [
              140484
            ],
            "artifact_refs": [
              "A8"
            ],
            "decision_refs": [],
            "reactions": [
              {
                "emoji": "heavy_check_mark",
                "count": 1
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "msg_id": "M26",
            "speaker_id": 128135,
            "reply_to": "M23",
            "text": "Ok, bottom two shelves for bulky. I will write that into the draft for T3. We should also add a rule about heavy items always on the bottom, even if they are not fragile.",
            "mentions": [
              27468
            ],
            "artifact_refs": [
              "T3"
            ],
            "decision_refs": [],
            "reactions": []
          },
          {
            "msg_id": "M27",
            "speaker_id": 213765,
            "reply_to": "M24",
            "text": "Ok, Zone F for flowers. I will write down the rules for A4. Do I need to worry about anything else?",
            "mentions": [
              27468
            ],
            "artifact_refs": [
              "A4"
            ],
            "decision_refs": [],
            "reactions": []
          },
          {
            "msg_id": "M28",
            "speaker_id": 27468,
            "reply_to": "M27",
            "text": "Just make sure the instructions in A4 align with the general handling guidelines from T3 that @128135 is working on. We need them to be consistent.",
            "mentions": [
              213765,
